# Netlify deploy (SOTS)

When the user says **push** (or wants changes live):

1. Commit relevant source files only (not `dist/`, `node_modules/`, `.tmp-*`, SEO HTML noise).
2. Push to **both** remotes on `main`:
   - `origin` → `https://github.com/tmanning0911/SOTS.git` (primary working repo)
   - `netlify` → `https://github.com/tmanning0911/ubiquitous-maamoul-8b9b7f.git` (**this** is what Netlify builds from)
3. Always run a production CLI deploy afterward (do not rely on GitHub auto-build alone):

```bash
git push origin HEAD && git push netlify HEAD:main
npx netlify deploy --prod --build
```

4. Confirm the linked Netlify project is **`ubiquitous-maamoul-8b9b7f`**  
   Live URL: https://ubiquitous-maamoul-8b9b7f.netlify.app  
   Admin: https://app.netlify.com/projects/ubiquitous-maamoul-8b9b7f

5. Do **not** assume `www.shakespeareonthesound.org` shows new work — that domain may still be on Wix until DNS cutover.

6. After deploy, confirm the production URL is live with the new commit when relevant.
